      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Looking back at this now, I don't think I explained it very well. I don't understand the \"offending mouth shape\", since, the way I see it, is that  it's going too far into the negative when I am not making any facial expression whatsoever. \n\n     If the only visme going into the negative is the \"aa\" shape, then should the exaggeration or expressiveness of the other shapes even matter? If my real face is at a true neutral expression, all other shapes should be at 0, or close to 0, right? All the other expressions are fine. It's just the neutral that's an issue.\n\n     Is it not possible, at least until this gets resolved, to make a simple toggle to remove our faces influence on the mouth, and let VRChat handle the mouth through audio detection like it has always been?\n\n     I genuinely enjoy using the Selfie Expression feature, but a lot of the avatars I like the use keep running into this issue, and so I end up not using it because it looks too goofy and unreliable. The eyetracking and blinking, along with head and torso movement is great! And those two features make it feel much more alive as it is.\n\n     I would be perfectly fine with leaving the mouth to audio influence while we wait for a true fix. It's been over a year now and this is something many of us would like to be fixed.",
